From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:24:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qup: Suspend through runtime PM in the late phase

qup_i2c_suspend() only turns the clocks off when the controller is
runtime-active, but qup_i2c_resume() always turns them on again, so a
controller that was runtime-suspended before system suspend comes back
with its core and AHB clocks enabled once more than its runtime PM
status says. Checking the runtime status again in resume isn't enough:
runtime PM is enabled again in the early resume phase, before the
normal-phase resume callback runs, and a client that transfers in that
window (a charger reading its fuel gauge after the cable was plugged in
during suspend) runtime-resumes the controller first. Resume then sees
an active controller and enables its clocks a second time.

Either way one enable count is never dropped. On MSM8996 the QUP core
clocks run from XO, so XO can't be released again and the RPM no
longer reaches vmin in any later suspend.

Let the PM core keep the books: pm_runtime_force_suspend() in the late
phase runtime-suspends the controller only if it is active and records
that, and pm_runtime_force_resume() in the early phase resumes only
what it suspended. A controller that is runtime-suspended stays off,
and later transfers resume it the normal way. This also closes the
window between the normal and the late suspend phases in which the
controller was off while its runtime PM status still said active.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c | 21 +--------------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
index ee7915ee2..1e5d020a2 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
@@ -1991,27 +1991,8 @@ static int qup_i2c_pm_resume_runtime(struct device *device)
 	return qup_i2c_enable_clocks(qup);
 }
 
-static int qup_i2c_suspend(struct device *device)
-{
-	if (!pm_runtime_suspended(device))
-		return qup_i2c_pm_suspend_runtime(device);
-	return 0;
-}
-
-static int qup_i2c_resume(struct device *device)
-{
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = qup_i2c_pm_resume_runtime(device);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	pm_request_autosuspend(device);
-	return 0;
-}
-
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qup_i2c_qup_pm_ops = {
-	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qup_i2c_suspend, qup_i2c_resume)
+	LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qup_i2c_pm_suspend_runtime,
 		       qup_i2c_pm_resume_runtime, NULL)
 };
